        {
          "record": "e733aad4-8e12-48cc-b940-1106ad8499a9",
          "statement": "video-plan takes --keyframes {off,chained,independent}, defaulting to off. 'off' attaches only each shot's finished frame F# and ignores keyframe pngs even when they are already on disk. 'independent' is the original S10 behaviour, safe only on a single-shot clip where no neighbour can be contradicted. 'chained' reserves the name for the successor design (each shot's opening anchor is the previous shot's accepted closing anchor) and raises keyframe_mode_not_implemented rather than silently behaving like something else, so flipping the default is not a dead end."
