          "statement": "Measured on the same engine the same day. Failing codes by attempt: live-action group-1 4/2/2, live-action group-2 8/4/5, stylised group-1 5/6/5/5. Live action roughly halves its defects at intensity 1 and then plateaus; the stylised clip never improves, with CANON_DRIFT and TEXT_GARBLED surviving every intensity while the others rotate, and intensity 3's simplification introducing HOOK_WEAK. Consequences: max-retries 1 is the right default for a stylised group, since attempt 2 bought nothing in three of four measured ladders and attempt 3 has twice made things worse (WRAPPER_SIZE on the image ladder, HOOK_WEAK on the video one); a stylised campaign's remaining defects are compositional rather than instructional and are fixed by writing different beats per the style manual's measured limits; and live action is where the ladder earns its cost, group-2 going from 8 failing codes to 4 for one 3.72 dollar attempt."
