          "statement": "Lane 2 must pass a simulation contract before ANY live spend, the same discipline as Lane 1's Phase B: real adcrush code, fake vendors, under adcrush-cli/simulation. New fakes: fake_speech.py (a SpeechProvider returning a tiny valid WAV plus deterministic synthetic word timings derived from character counts, recording voice id, timestamps and previous_text/next_text), and fake_kie extended with the two ElevenLabs slugs. NO ffmpeg fake and NO sfx fake -- ASS burning and audio mixing are precisely what a fake would hide, and sfx arrive inside the fake clip's own audio track as they do in production. Eleven scenarios: captions_voice_over, voice_over_silent_plate, unwanted_speech, captions_lipsync, captions_both, fully_muted, caption_substyles, unsafe_copy, v3_timing_trade, handles_and_trim, model_tiering, keyframes_off, hook_weak. New checks include check_generate_audio_matches_resolution, check_prompt_forbids_dialogue_in_tts_mode, check_ass_is_valid_and_timed, check_captions_use_real_word_timings, check_no_generator_text_requested, check_speech_gate_blocks_before_submit and check_assembled_duration_matches_brief."
