        {
          "record": "7dde0fd8-80a2-44bf-9aa6-0adcb4bb2c51",
          "statement": "video.assemble_final_video takes audio= and speech_provider=. When audio.layers.resolve(...).speech is tts or both it renders one narration segment per block via audio/providers.py, places each at an explicit adelay through audio/mix.place_segments, ducks the clip's own bed to BED_GAIN 0.35 with mix_narration (never replaces it -- the provider's audio flag stays on for sfx), and records runs/<rev>/video/narration/narration.json. The DELAY for each block is the same number that block's first caption starts on (captions.edl.block_offsets), so audio and captions cannot drift: one derivation, used twice. Ordering is plan captions -> render narration -> adopt measured timings -> burn; burning first would freeze the planner's estimate into the deliverable while the real read was already known. No provider is constructed unless the run is --live --yes, so a dry run still produces the cut and reports the skip in the ledger."
