      "id": "narrator-reads-the-on-screen-copy",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "7dde0fd8-80a2-44bf-9aa6-0adcb4bb2c51",
          "statement": "captions.edl.caption_lines is the single predicate for 'this line is on screen' (modes cartela and narration), and video.narration_segments projects from it rather than applying its own rule. In a voice-over ad the on-screen copy IS the script, and every project written before the narration mode existed keeps its copy in cartela -- selecting only narration rendered nothing on the canonical scenario. dialogo is excluded: the video model performs a character speaking in shot. A line whose printed form does not normalise and that carries no voice_over is skipped rather than guessed at; speech_safety.check is what surfaces those."
        }
