    {
      "id": "no-generator-is-asked-for-text",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "6f17b960-53a5-4b10-8d38-f4dd650ddb8f",
          "statement": "Every generator is now told there is no text in frame beyond what is physically printed on the product: the video prompt unconditionally, compile._dialogue_section (captions and narration removed, only performed speech survives because it changes the pose), _caption_mode_section (returns nothing), and keyframes.caption_for (always None, because a lettered keyframe becomes a reference teaching the video model to letter too). Copy reaches a video prompt only as a spoken cue, and only when the video model is the one speaking -- otherwise the clip would speak over the narration laid on top. On the judge side the 'required caption present and correctly spelled' question is gone, which is what produced five false TEXT_GARBLED flags on one live pass, two over the confidence gate and each costing a render, because a caption fading in over the first second looks missing in a sampled frame. TEXT_BURNED_IN now means ANY text not printed on the product; TEXT_GARBLED narrows to product lettering, which still matters because a misspelled pack is a brand defect."
