    {
      "id": "print-critical-references",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "0ffda16f-bd54-414f-aff8-950ee3b90efb",
          "statement": "CanonElement.print_critical declares that an element carries printed copy which must be reproduced exactly, so its SHEET is the only source of that wording. build_reference_plan ranks print-critical sheets ahead of every other canon sheet, so reference truncation cannot reach them; canon generate --print-critical sets it. Declared rather than inferred from the description, for the same reason face_policy is: reading prose for the word 'copy' fails silently and in English only. Excluded from compute_element_hash -- a fact about how the element must be REFERENCED, not about what the art is -- so declaring it never forces a billed re-render. The underlying principle: a shape survives being described ('a low flat square slab, width clearly greater than thickness' is actionable prose and the shape-lock bullets work), but thirteen lines of pack copy reach a generator as thirteen chances to invent. Reference priority is therefore not one fixed order; it depends on whether the fact a sheet carries can travel in words at all."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "product-truth-beats-invention",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "c8575d29-c8df-44f8-94c9-8a844faaab01",
          "statement": "At the canon gate the expand LLM's product descriptions were overridden with the approved product truth: it had proposed a 3cm rounded chew with a small wordmark where the real chew is a flat 2.5cm square under all-over tiled foil. The papercraft reference reel renders the chew as a ROUND rosette; the canon keeps the real flat square and carries the rosette as a die-cut pattern on its top face. The real 30-count pouch is DARK COFFEE-BROWN with a gold front panel, NOT black: both new projects' pouch canon was regenerated with the full front copy transcribed from the photo. This matters beyond the sheet, because the description feeds the judge's rubric -- 'black pouch' would make the judge flag a correct render as CANON_DRIFT and burn video retries. coffee-chews-ugc-v2's youchews_retail_bag_sealed still says black and should be corrected."
        }
