    {
      "id": "resumable-stages-need-a-driver",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "aa8c35e7-5bc3-4721-b1d5-4c351904b4a5",
          "statement": "render-assembly and keyframes take --no-wait, --poll-interval and --max-wait, and wait by default. Each underlying cycle is ONE bounded pass that submits, reports what is in flight as pending, and returns; the --review stages are driven to completion by media_review.loop.run_until_settled, but these two had no driver. A single call therefore left everything pending, and a runbook that stepped straight on to video-plan planned WITHOUT the G# and K# references those stages exist to produce. cli._drive_to_completion repeats the pass until nothing is pending, it halts, or max_wait expires; each pass is idempotent and never resubmits an in-flight job."
        }
