    {
      "id": "shape-lock-bullets-rank-print-critical",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "c603706e-d53d-4e61-a620-4c9b947a5f01",
          "statement": "_shape_lock_bullets states print-critical elements first and MAX_SHAPE_LOCK_BULLETS is 5 (was 3). Taking the first N in reference order let three chew-and-wrapper elements fill the cap while the retail pouch -- the hero prop of the failing shot -- had no constraint line anywhere in the prompt. The cap is a length guard, not a ranking; 5 bullets cost about 200 characters against 2.3k of headroom under the 6k budget. Same principle as the reference plan one layer up. The fallback chain already reaches physical_profile.must, so an element carrying only a positive must does get a line -- the ingredient set's counts had simply been cut by the same cap, which is why it came back with five beans and an invented halved coconut."
        }
