      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "65ab88dd-ed3a-43ce-a5b4-6f409d448e74",
          "statement": "build_reference_plan takes style= and promotes the FIRST shot's F# to just after the storyboards when compile.is_stylised_medium(style). Without it a nine-slot model filled up with G + three B sheets + five canon sheets and dropped every final, leaving the video model with sketches and plainly-lit turntables and no example of the medium -- the same failure the image lane had one stage upstream. The original 'finals last' ordering was reasoned on a photoreal campaign, where the canon sheets already are the look, and that case keeps it. is_stylised_medium is shared with canon_precedence_clause so the two cannot disagree about what stylised means."
        }
