    {
      "id": "elevenlabs-family-outage",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "c04f61e7-cc43-4b8f-a400-3cdb3dd1905e",
          "statement": "Five isolated REST submissions bypassing kie-cli and the pipeline. v3 dialogue with voice 'Phil' returned 422 at SUBMIT ('Invalid voice parameter: Phil'); v3 with the voice id LG95yZDEHg6fCZdQjLqj submitted 200 and terminated fail/500; v2 with the name, with the id, and with the minimal documented payload all submitted 200 and terminated fail/500. Credits refunded to 0.0 on every failure. Image and video jobs on the same key completed normally within minutes, so the account and key are fine. text-to-dialogue-v3 therefore fails exactly like text-to-speech-multilingual-v2 and switching models is NOT a workaround. Before failing, v3 metered 0.28 credits against v2's 12.0 for the same single line -- a lead on narration cost worth verifying once the endpoint recovers, not a fact to plan on, since it was read off a job that then failed."
        }
      ],
