        {
          "record": "2ebc9955-2941-4468-81ad-2484f022cfc4",
          "statement": "video-assemble on rev-003 produced final.mp4 at 15.136s measured against 15.0 planned (single group, no join trim), 9 caption events burned through the ass filter, caption_timings estimated. The narration degradation worked in production: narration.failed = speech_failed carrying kie's 500 Internal Error, with the cut and captions delivered anyway and a re-run note. The video ladder settled exhausted, promoting attempt 1, with failing-code counts by attempt of 5, 6, 5, 5 -- it did NOT converge, and attempt 3 introduced HOOK_WEAK, the documented cost of intensity 3 simplifying a beat. Budget: 4 submits (1488 credits, 14.88 dollars), 4 judge calls, 1 synth call. This is the third bug in the caption subsystem that only reading pixels would find, after the missing Style: prefix and the ass_time carry."
        }
