  "items": [
    {
      "id": "captions-as-post-process",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "bc45b217-2f22-46e8-b2fe-436b0e4d5c27",
          "statement": "Captions move out of the generator into a deterministic post-step: own a captions module that writes ASS (Advanced SubStation Alpha) from the EDL plus the style's caption_style, burned with ffmpeg's 'ass' filter, NOT the 'subtitles' filter which discards animation. ASS gives per-word karaoke timing, outline, shadow, font, size, colour and absolute positioning, i.e. the CapCut/TikTok look with real control, and ffmpeg is already a hard dependency. Deliberately NOT adopting ai-video-captions, captionforge or similar: they are all transcription-first (Whisper then ASS), and we already hold the exact caption text and timecodes, so transcription would only add a dependency and inject recognition error. Second-order win: with captions in post, both image and video prompts can demand no text at all, so TEXT_GARBLED and TEXT_BURNED_IN stop being failure classes the generator can fail on -- a direct attack on the retry ladder that dominates cost. StyleProfile.on_screen_text changes meaning to 'burn captions in post' and caption_style becomes a struct."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "coffee-chews-ugc-campaign",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "0f79ce0b-fcba-4c13-a0df-950174da407f",
          "statement": "First real campaign built with adcrush: YouChews Coffee Chews 30s/9:16 UGC-vertical Reel, 6 blocks, real brand assets from Google Drive, all rendered cleanly in rev-002. PDF export committed to research/coffee-chews-ugc-reel/. Creative iteration and M-E per-style validation remain open."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hooks-and-assembly-trim",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "bc45b217-2f22-46e8-b2fe-436b0e4d5c27",
          "statement": "Two further changes. (1) Hooks: the first 5 seconds get their own contract. NarrativeFormat.hook_required already exists and is NEVER read -- dead config to be enforced: expand writes a hook_device on block 1, the judge scores the first shot against a hook rubric (subject readable within one second, movement in the first half-second, a visual question), and a new HOOK_WEAK code gets its own recipe ladder; block 1's image prompts bias toward higher contrast and a tighter subject. (2) Assembly trim: trim a default 0.5s at every internal join (tail of clip N, head of clip N+1), parametrizable via --trim-seconds and assembly.trim_seconds. Caution: trimming shortens the total, so a two-group 30s ad lands near 29s -- either report the real duration or design the EDL so each group's last half-second is a held handle. Silently delivering 29s for a 30s brief is exactly the drift this project exists to remove."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "keyframes-off-by-default",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "bc45b217-2f22-46e8-b2fe-436b0e4d5c27",
          "statement": "S10 keyframe triplets are to be OFF by default; pass the block's finished frame as the single anchor. Observed failure: the beat where the talent enters the car reads as two different cars. Cause: a triplet imposes three hard anchors per shot (nine per 3-shot clip plus the clip endpoints) and each block's triplet is planned INDEPENDENTLY from its own final frame, so block-4's last frame and block-5's first frame are unrelated renders of the same place and the model resolves the contradiction by cutting to a different car. Generalisation: any per-item reference generation must either be CHAINED from the previous item's accepted output or not used at all -- independently generated anchors are worse than fewer anchors. Keep the triplet as an opt-in for single-shot clips, where there is no neighbour to contradict."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lane-2-staged-plan",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "959aa213-0dc1-4576-b2d9-340c2d6cdeb5",
          "statement": "Lane 2 is planned in docs/plans/captions-audio-and-hooks.md, seven stages ordered by leverage per dollar because measurement showed re-rendering, not model choice, dominates cost (one group's four-attempt ladder was $37.80 of a $50.85 ad). Stage 1 stops the bleeding: keyframes off by default, a parametrizable join trim, and model TIERING rather than downgrading. Stage 2 classifies audio intent. Stage 3 builds deterministic ASS captions. Stage 4 adds voice-over-safe copy. Stage 5 integrates ElevenLabs narration with a tagged voice catalog and a preview view. Stage 6 makes the hook a contract. Stage 7 is the integrator."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "reference-anchors-must-be-chained",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "959aa213-0dc1-4576-b2d9-340c2d6cdeb5",
          "statement": "New general rule from the car-teleport artefact: per-item reference generation must either be CHAINED, each item derived from the previous item's accepted output, or not used at all, because independently generated anchors are worse than fewer anchors. A keyframe triplet imposes three hard anchors per shot (nine per 3-shot clip plus the clip endpoints) and each block's triplet was planned independently of its neighbours, so consecutive anchors were unrelated renders of the same place and the model cut to a different car. video-plan gains --keyframes {off,chained,independent} defaulting to off; 'chained' reserves the name for the upgrade so the default change is not a dead end; 'independent' preserves today's behaviour for single-shot clips where there is no neighbour to contradict."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "reusable-cli-ad-creative",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "ea50dbdb-ef7f-4530-9514-faa64f5c1a42",
          "statement": "Design a reusable, LLM-agnostic (OpenAI/Anthropic), 100%% CLI, no-agent system (adcrush) for authoring and publishing ad-creative storyboard image sets, generalized from the 29-razones reference implementation, with a future image-to-video lane explicitly deferred."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tier-the-video-model",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "bc45b217-2f22-46e8-b2fe-436b0e4d5c27",
          "statement": "Baseline model policy, corrected by measurement. KEEP gpt-image-2-5-sunburst for images: it costs the same 10 credits as gpt-image-2 and is visibly better, so downgrading saves nothing. DO move video off seedance-2.5 as the default: 372 vs 945 credits for the same 15s 720p clip. The real trade-off is references, not price -- seedance-2/-2-fast accept 9 reference images against 2.5's 30 and cap at 15s, and one group's prompt already carried 16 references, so seven would be dropped with a warning, a canon-fidelity regression. Preferred shape: tier it with --draft-model and --final-model, running the judge/retry ladder cheap and promoting the accepted cut once on the expensive model, mirroring the Flare/Sunburst split already in place for images. A four-attempt group then costs $14.88 plus one $9.45 final render instead of $37.80."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "video-gen-lane",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "7828b659-1b1d-4d5b-b8ed-6a1aa4091623",
          "statement": "Implemented the long-deferred image-to-video lane: video.py (clustering/prompt assembly/reference selection/hash-lock/async cycle), async_jobs.py (shared credit-halt/retry extraction), kie.submit_video(), new CLI+MCP surfaces. Validated against real Coffee Chews rev-002 data (clean 2x15s groups, 6 refs each, zero warnings). 168 tests passing. Real --live --yes submission smoke test still needs explicit user authorization."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "video-self-improvement-goal",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "8a13cafe-b985-40f2-9eb0-6ef90a61700e",
          "statement": "Render 15s video blocks reliably and know without human frame-scrubbing whether they succeeded, proven by one budget-capped live pass on campaigns/coffee-chews-ugc-reel (<=3 retries/group) after a full offline simulation passes."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "voice-over-safe-copy",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "bc45b217-2f22-46e8-b2fe-436b0e4d5c27",
          "statement": "Printed form and spoken form are two different fields and conflating them is the same class of error as conflating a canon id with a description. Add DialogueLine.voice_over alongside text, plus a DETERMINISTIC pre-flight that fails before any video render when a spoken line contains a token that does not read aloud correctly: unit abbreviations (mg, g, oz, ml, kg), digit-group separators (1,095), currency, percent, ranges, initialisms (USA, TM) and URLs. Ship a normaliser for common cases and require an explicit voice_over for anything it cannot handle -- never silently guess. This lets the printed caption stay tight ('100mg caffeine. 25 calories. 2g sugar.') while the voice-over reads naturally."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    }
  ],
