          "statement": "S10 keyframe triplets are to be OFF by default; pass the block's finished frame as the single anchor. Observed failure: the beat where the talent enters the car reads as two different cars. Cause: a triplet imposes three hard anchors per shot (nine per 3-shot clip plus the clip endpoints) and each block's triplet is planned INDEPENDENTLY from its own final frame, so block-4's last frame and block-5's first frame are unrelated renders of the same place and the model resolves the contradiction by cutting to a different car. Generalisation: any per-item reference generation must either be CHAINED from the previous item's accepted output or not used at all -- independently generated anchors are worse than fewer anchors. Keep the triplet as an opt-in for single-shot clips, where there is no neighbour to contradict."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lane-2-staged-plan",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "959aa213-0dc1-4576-b2d9-340c2d6cdeb5",
          "statement": "Lane 2 is planned in docs/plans/captions-audio-and-hooks.md, seven stages ordered by leverage per dollar because measurement showed re-rendering, not model choice, dominates cost (one group's four-attempt ladder was $37.80 of a $50.85 ad). Stage 1 stops the bleeding: keyframes off by default, a parametrizable join trim, and model TIERING rather than downgrading. Stage 2 classifies audio intent. Stage 3 builds deterministic ASS captions. Stage 4 adds voice-over-safe copy. Stage 5 integrates ElevenLabs narration with a tagged voice catalog and a preview view. Stage 6 makes the hook a contract. Stage 7 is the integrator."
        }
      ],
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "id": "reference-anchors-must-be-chained",
      "alternatives": [
        {
          "record": "959aa213-0dc1-4576-b2d9-340c2d6cdeb5",
          "statement": "New general rule from the car-teleport artefact: per-item reference generation must either be CHAINED, each item derived from the previous item's accepted output, or not used at all, because independently generated anchors are worse than fewer anchors. A keyframe triplet imposes three hard anchors per shot (nine per 3-shot clip plus the clip endpoints) and each block's triplet was planned independently of its neighbours, so consecutive anchors were unrelated renders of the same place and the model cut to a different car. video-plan gains --keyframes {off,chained,independent} defaulting to off; 'chained' reserves the name for the upgrade so the default change is not a dead end; 'independent' preserves today's behaviour for single-shot clips where there is no neighbour to contradict."
        }
