          "statement": "Baseline model policy, corrected by measurement. KEEP gpt-image-2-5-sunburst for images: it costs the same 10 credits as gpt-image-2 and is visibly better, so downgrading saves nothing. DO move video off seedance-2.5 as the default: 372 vs 945 credits for the same 15s 720p clip. The real trade-off is references, not price -- seedance-2/-2-fast accept 9 reference images against 2.5's 30 and cap at 15s, and one group's prompt already carried 16 references, so seven would be dropped with a warning, a canon-fidelity regression. Preferred shape: tier it with --draft-model and --final-model, running the judge/retry ladder cheap and promoting the accepted cut once on the expensive model, mirroring the Flare/Sunburst split already in place for images. A four-attempt group then costs $14.88 plus one $9.45 final render instead of $37.80."
