          "statement": "Printed form and spoken form are two different fields and conflating them is the same class of error as conflating a canon id with a description. Add DialogueLine.voice_over alongside text, plus a DETERMINISTIC pre-flight that fails before any video render when a spoken line contains a token that does not read aloud correctly: unit abbreviations (mg, g, oz, ml, kg), digit-group separators (1,095), currency, percent, ranges, initialisms (USA, TM) and URLs. Ship a normaliser for common cases and require an explicit voice_over for anything it cannot handle -- never silently guess. This lets the printed caption stay tight ('100mg caffeine. 25 calories. 2g sugar.') while the voice-over reads naturally."
